UID:stanford_campus-localist-53759577709275-53759577710301@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the speaker for coffee\, cookies\, and conversation befor
 e the talk\, starting at 11:45am.\n\nNeural circuits for natural vision Ab
 stract\n\nNatural visual processing entails a complex interplay between se
 nsory input\, behavioral context\, and on-going brain dynamics. Our lab se
 eks to understand how these processes give rise to goal-directed visual be
 haviors\, by exploring the neural circuits mediating ethologically relevan
 t behaviors that laboratory mice perform\, including prey capture and dist
 ance\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://neuroscience.stanford.edu/node/579
 9\nLast synced: 2026-11-05 12:29 PST
LOCATION:Stanford Neurosciences Building
URL:https://neuroscience.stanford.edu/node/5799
END:VEVENT
