DTSTAMP:20261105T202933Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54045874768748-54045879283745@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Slow slip and nonvolcanic tremor were discovered over 20 years
  ago\, but we still don’t understand how they are generated\, or what di
 stinguishes fault zones that produce slow slip from those that produce “
 regular” earthquakes. Models of slow slip tend to come in 2 flavors: \n
 \nContinuum elastic/frictional models\, designed to reproduce their slow p
 ropagation speeds and faster “tremor reversals”\, and stochastic Brown
 ian walk models\, which lack basic physics but which reproduce various sta
 tistical pro\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-05 12:29 PST
LOCATION:Mitchell Earth Sciences
END:VEVENT
