BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Structured Liberal Education (SLE)] SLE Salon: Orlando Reade Expl
 ores How Paradise Lost Has Influenced Political Struggles and Revolutionar
 y Movements over the Past 400 Years
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T173000
DTSTAMP:20261105T202933Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54284955023230-54284955024255@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Drawing from his own experiences teaching Paradise Lost in New
  Jersey prisons\, English scholar Orlando Reade deftly investigates how th
 e poem was read by people embedded in struggles against tyranny\, slavery
 \, colonialism\, gender inequality\, and capitalist exploitation. It is ex
 perimental nonfiction at its finest\; rich literary analysis and social\, 
 cultural\, and political history are woven together to make a clarifying c
 ase for the undeniable impact of the poem.\n\nLearn more about Orlando Rea
 de he\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-05 12:29 PST
LOCATION:Florence Moore Hall\, SLE Main Lounge
END:VEVENT
